iterations.notes:
I'm proposing 53 tasks, with nothing checked yet: 30 in living_dining_kitchen and 23 in the bedroom. The bedroom only has 9 pickable objects, so I stopped at 23 there rather than pad it with near-copies.

Expected sorting (your checker decides):
(a) Likely bucket 1: the four measured grasps (coffee canister on the cart, jam on the island, TV remote on the coffee table, dish soap on the long counter at 6/10). Also two short carries built on those grasps (remote to the sofa, canister to the island), plus objects of similar size on the same or similar surfaces: DVD remote, pattern-3 candle, coffee can on the dining table.
(b) Likely bucket 2. The skills these would point to:
- placing on a surface (on_surface_single is untested; motor_put_back only measured 0.3-0.8 m), for the remote to the TV stand, jam, canister, clock, cookbook, vase and hand soap;
- placing into a container (into_container_single_arm is untested), for the fruit bowls, utensil tray, pot, trash bin and candle dishes;
- grasping and placing under a shelf above (overhead open_above is under 0.6 m), for the wolf figurine, cookbook, vases, small plant, novels and the bedroom bottom/middle display shelves;
- the known grasp failures (white mug 2/10, wallet 0/10, thick novel 0/10).
(c) Likely bucket 3:
- support surfaces at or below 0.22 m (white vase on the bookcase's bottom shelf, remote to the coffee table's lower shelf, plant to the nightstand's bottom shelf);
- support at 1.07-1.22 m (top display-unit candle, black wall shelf), above where motor_grasp support_top lifts (0.3-0.8 m);
- the nightstand's middle shelf, with only 0.14 m clear above it;
- surfaces the robot can't stand at (white dressing table, floating shelves);
- the car key: 0.015 m tall, below object_height_lifted 0.03, and top_down grasps were 0/3.

Every bedroom task also has a navigation gap. cross_room is untested, and the bedroom's spawn region had no reachable point at body radius 0.35 m. So bedroom tasks will probably be at least bucket 2, needing navigate.narrow_passage at radius 0.26. I proposed them anyway because they show which skills the bedroom would unlock.

Assumption on near(): it is measured in xy, but I don't know whether it is taken to the surface centre or its edge. So I used d = 0.8-1.0 m for surfaces (sofa seat, kitchen island, bed) and 0.3 m only when Y is an object.
